 "id": "1-3-0",
 "title": "Population, Migration and Urbanisation",
 "emoji": "👥",
 "cards": [
  {
   "tag": "Why this matters",
   "h": "People are the resource and the problem",
   "b": "<p>India became the world's most populous country in 2023 (UN estimate). Numbers decide <b>seats</b>, <b>grants</b>, schemes and the economy. Age profile creates the <b>demographic dividend</b>. UPSC asks about trends, regional contrasts, migration and cities.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Key figures",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 218\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"110\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Indicator</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"6\" width=\"190\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">India (source)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"32\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Population</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"32\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.21 bn (2011); about 1.4 bn now</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Density</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"62\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">382 per sq km (2011)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"92\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Sex ratio</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"92\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">943 (2011), 1,020 (NFHS-5)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Literacy</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"122\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">74% (2011)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"152\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">TFR</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"152\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.0 (NFHS-5, 2019-21)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"182\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"201\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Urban share</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"182\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"201\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">31% (2011)</text></svg><p>Population growth has slowed. The fertility rate is now below the replacement level of 2.1. The census due in 2021 was delayed by COVID-19; the next census was announced for 2027 with caste enumeration (as of the 2025 notification).</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Demographic transition",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 190\"><path d=\"M20 30 L60 30 L100 40 L160 80 L220 130 L300 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M20 140 L60 140 L110 120 L170 120 L220 135 L300 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"165\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stage 1</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"165\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stage 2</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"165\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stage 3</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"165\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stage 4</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"24\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\">Birth rate</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"108\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\">Death rate</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"184\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gap between lines: fast growth. India is in late stage 3.</text></svg><p><b>Stage 1</b>: high births, high deaths. <b>Stage 2</b>: deaths fall first, population booms. <b>Stage 3</b>: births fall. <b>Stage 4</b>: low births, low deaths. Some add a fifth stage of ageing and decline (Japan). India's states are in different stages: Kerala and Tamil Nadu are late; Bihar and Uttar Pradesh are earlier.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Demographic dividend and ageing",
   "b": "<p>A <b>dividend</b> arises when the working age (15-64) share is high. India's window runs to about 2040-50. It pays only if there are <b>jobs, skills and health</b>. Otherwise it is a \"demographic burden\". Southern states are ageing faster, with elderly share rising.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Migration",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 138\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"47.5\" y=\"29.0\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Push</text><rect x=\"91\" y=\"6\" width=\"219\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.5\" y=\"29.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Poverty, low wages, drought, conflict</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"47.5\" y=\"73.0\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Pull</text><rect x=\"91\" y=\"50\" width=\"219\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.5\" y=\"73.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jobs, wages, services, schools, safety</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"94\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"47.5\" y=\"117.0\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Pattern</text><rect x=\"91\" y=\"94\" width=\"219\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.5\" y=\"117.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rural to urban, UP and Bihar to Delhi, Maharashtra, Gujarat</text></svg><p>The 2011 Census counted about 45.6 crore migrants (37% of the population), mostly women moving for marriage. Men migrate for work. The 2020 lockdown exposed circular migrants' fragility; the <b>One Nation One Ration Card</b> and e-Shram portal followed.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Urbanisation",
   "b": "<p>The urban share was 31% in 2011 and is estimated around mid-30s now. Cities: Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata (the three mega-cities of 2011), then Chennai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad. A <b>census town</b> has 5,000 people, 75% non-farm male workers and density 400 per sq km. Problems: slums, traffic, floods, pollution, weak municipal finance.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Regional pattern of growth and density",
   "b": "<p>The Gangetic plains, coasts and Kerala are densely settled; deserts, Himalaya and the Northeast are thin. Uttar Pradesh is the largest state by population; Sikkim is the smallest. <b>Bihar</b> has the highest density among states (1,106 per sq km in 2011); Arunachal Pradesh the lowest. Reasons: fertile alluvium, water, history of farming, and now job-centres. Low density in hill states reflects relief and climate.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Debate",
   "h": "Delimitation and population control",
   "b": "<p>Seats in the Lok Sabha are frozen on 1971 numbers until the first census after 2026 (Articles 82 and 170). If seats follow today's population, northern states with higher growth gain and southern states lose share, though they did better at population control. The debate is about fairness: should success in family planning be penalised?</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Indian angle",
   "h": "Schemes and planning",
   "b": "<p><b>Smart Cities</b> (2015), <b>AMRUT</b> (2015, urban water), <b>Swachh Bharat</b> (2014), <b>PM Awas</b>, and <b>Mission Shakti</b> for women. The National Population Policy 2000 set the goal of reaching replacement TFR; <b>Mission Parivar Vikas</b> targets high-fertility districts. Regional contrasts: Kerala sex ratio above 1,000; Haryana among the lowest.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Exam lens",
   "cls": "exam",
   "h": "How to write this",
   "b": "<div class=\"box\"><h4>Likely questions</h4><p>\"Discuss the main features of India's demographic transition and the demographic dividend.\" (15 marks)</p><p>\"Examine the causes and consequences of rural-urban migration.\" (10 marks)</p></div><p><b>Structure:</b> data; theory; regional contrasts; opportunities and risks; schemes.</p><p><b>Prelims tip:</b> Census 2011 literacy is 74.04%, sex ratio 943; the replacement level TFR is 2.1.</p>"
  }
 ],
